    {
      "id": "G1-realized-observation",
      "source_id": "gneiting-raftery-2007",
      "text": "Scoring rules assess the quality of probabilistic forecasts, by assigning a numerical score based on the predictive distribution and on the\n           event or value that materializes.",
      "location": "Abstract; journal p359",
      "pdf_page": 1,
      "extracted_text_offset": 217,
      "raw_sha256": "d31a0c5f0ae8fec1a0a6544db5d056645b2d7296d71b44a2e8efb293c7d87ba2",
      "extracted_text_sha256": "80c52fd988b1a3639b75100dbf998f3943e73fc91177a1195627f2224060372e"
    },
    {
      "id": "G2-strict-properness",
      "source_id": "gneiting-raftery-2007",
      "text": "It is strictly proper if the maximum is unique.",
      "location": "Abstract; journal p359",
      "pdf_page": 1,
      "extracted_text_offset": 604,
      "raw_sha256": "d31a0c5f0ae8fec1a0a6544db5d056645b2d7296d71b44a2e8efb293c7d87ba2",
      "extracted_text_sha256": "80c52fd988b1a3639b75100dbf998f3943e73fc91177a1195627f2224060372e"
    },
    {
      "id": "G3-brier",
      "source_id": "gneiting-raftery-2007",
      "text": "Example 1 (Quadratic or Brier score).",
      "location": "Section 3.1, Example 1; journal p363",
      "pdf_page": 5,
      "extracted_text_offset": 33270,
      "raw_sha256": "d31a0c5f0ae8fec1a0a6544db5d056645b2d7296d71b44a2e8efb293c7d87ba2",
      "extracted_text_sha256": "80c52fd988b1a3639b75100dbf998f3943e73fc91177a1195627f2224060372e"
    },
    {
      "id": "G4-brier-indicator",
      "source_id": "gneiting-raftery-2007",
      "text": "where δij = 1 if i = j and δij = 0 otherwise.",
      "location": "Section 3.1, Example 1; journal p363",
      "pdf_page": 5,
      "extracted_text_offset": 34156,
      "raw_sha256": "d31a0c5f0ae8fec1a0a6544db5d056645b2d7296d71b44a2e8efb293c7d87ba2",
      "extracted_text_sha256": "80c52fd988b1a3639b75100dbf998f3943e73fc91177a1195627f2224060372e"
    },
    {
      "id": "G5-log-formula",
      "source_id": "gneiting-raftery-2007",
      "text": "S(p, i) = log pi .",
      "location": "Section 3.1, Example 3; journal p363",
      "pdf_page": 5,
      "extracted_text_offset": 37298,
      "raw_sha256": "d31a0c5f0ae8fec1a0a6544db5d056645b2d7296d71b44a2e8efb293c7d87ba2",
      "extracted_text_sha256": "80c52fd988b1a3639b75100dbf998f3943e73fc91177a1195627f2224060372e"
    },
    {
      "id": "G6-log-unbounded",
      "source_id": "gneiting-raftery-2007",
      "text": "the logarithmic score has been criticized for its unboundedness,",
      "location": "Section 3.1, Example 3; journal p363",
      "pdf_page": 5,
      "extracted_text_offset": 38294,
      "raw_sha256": "d31a0c5f0ae8fec1a0a6544db5d056645b2d7296d71b44a2e8efb293c7d87ba2",
      "extracted_text_sha256": "80c52fd988b1a3639b75100dbf998f3943e73fc91177a1195627f2224060372e"
    },
    {
      "id": "G7-zero-event",
      "source_id": "gneiting-raftery-2007",
      "text": "S(0, 1) = −∞",
      "location": "Section 3.2, boundary allowance; journal p363",
      "pdf_page": 5,
      "extracted_text_offset": 37595,
      "raw_sha256": "d31a0c5f0ae8fec1a0a6544db5d056645b2d7296d71b44a2e8efb293c7d87ba2",
      "extracted_text_sha256": "80c52fd988b1a3639b75100dbf998f3943e73fc91177a1195627f2224060372e"
    },
    {
      "id": "G8-pre-observation",
      "source_id": "gneiting-raftery-2007",
      "text": "specified before any of the Xi ’s are observed; that is, there are",
      "location": "Section 7.1, fully specified forecasting rule; journal p372",
      "pdf_page": 14,
      "extracted_text_offset": 101249,
      "raw_sha256": "d31a0c5f0ae8fec1a0a6544db5d056645b2d7296d71b44a2e8efb293c7d87ba2",
      "extracted_text_sha256": "80c52fd988b1a3639b75100dbf998f3943e73fc91177a1195627f2224060372e"
    },
    {
      "id": "G9-low-probability",
      "source_id": "gneiting-raftery-2007",
      "text": "proper but involves a harsh penalty for low probability events",
      "location": "Section 8.2; journal p374",
      "pdf_page": 16,
      "extracted_text_offset": 121169,
      "raw_sha256": "d31a0c5f0ae8fec1a0a6544db5d056645b2d7296d71b44a2e8efb293c7d87ba2",
      "extracted_text_sha256": "80c52fd988b1a3639b75100dbf998f3943e73fc91177a1195627f2224060372e"
    },
    {
      "id": "C1-time-process",
      "source_id": "sklearn-cross-validation",
      "text": "If one knows that the samples have been generated using a time-dependent process, it is safer to use a time-series aware cross-validation scheme .",
      "location": "Section 3.1.2.1",
      "pdf_page": null,
      "extracted_text_offset": 14711,
      "raw_sha256": "78d7587fa92ba3b3e480c9d841b50fedc14ac29d571ccb319d4068235154f0e2",
      "extracted_text_sha256": "009ce290e0897fddf43ed8ad55821d68c586cde2992b8d654e1e943363144e6d"
    },
    {
      "id": "C2-group-structure",
      "source_id": "sklearn-cross-validation",
      "text": "Similarly, if we know that the generative process has a group structure (samples collected from different subjects, experiments, measurement devices), it is safer to use group-wise cross-validation .",
      "location": "Section 3.1.2.1",
      "pdf_page": null,
      "extracted_text_offset": 14858,
      "raw_sha256": "78d7587fa92ba3b3e480c9d841b50fedc14ac29d571ccb319d4068235154f0e2",
      "extracted_text_sha256": "009ce290e0897fddf43ed8ad55821d68c586cde2992b8d654e1e943363144e6d"
    },
    {
      "id": "C3-group-holdout",
      "source_id": "sklearn-cross-validation",
      "text": "GroupKFold is a variation of K-fold which ensures that the same group is not represented in both testing and training sets.",
      "location": "Section 3.1.2.4.1 Group k-fold",
      "pdf_page": null,
      "extracted_text_offset": 25387,
      "raw_sha256": "78d7587fa92ba3b3e480c9d841b50fedc14ac29d571ccb319d4068235154f0e2",
      "extracted_text_sha256": "009ce290e0897fddf43ed8ad55821d68c586cde2992b8d654e1e943363144e6d"
    },
    {
      "id": "C4-time-correlation",
      "source_id": "sklearn-cross-validation",
      "text": "Time series data is characterized by the correlation between observations that are near in time ( autocorrelation ).",
      "location": "Section 3.1.2.6",
      "pdf_page": null,
      "extracted_text_offset": 33464,
      "raw_sha256": "78d7587fa92ba3b3e480c9d841b50fedc14ac29d571ccb319d4068235154f0e2",
      "extracted_text_sha256": "009ce290e0897fddf43ed8ad55821d68c586cde2992b8d654e1e943363144e6d"
    },
    {
      "id": "C5-future",
      "source_id": "sklearn-cross-validation",
      "text": "Therefore, it is very important to evaluate our model for time series data on the “future” observations least like those that are used to train the model.",
      "location": "Section 3.1.2.6",
      "pdf_page": null,
      "extracted_text_offset": 33878,
      "raw_sha256": "78d7587fa92ba3b3e480c9d841b50fedc14ac29d571ccb319d4068235154f0e2",
      "extracted_text_sha256": "009ce290e0897fddf43ed8ad55821d68c586cde2992b8d654e1e943363144e6d"
    },
    {
      "id": "C6-fixed-intervals",
      "source_id": "sklearn-cross-validation",
      "text": "This class can be used to cross-validate time series data samples that are observed at fixed time intervals.",
      "location": "Section 3.1.2.6.1 Time Series Split",
      "pdf_page": null,
      "extracted_text_offset": 34480,
      "raw_sha256": "78d7587fa92ba3b3e480c9d841b50fedc14ac29d571ccb319d4068235154f0e2",
      "extracted_text_sha256": "009ce290e0897fddf43ed8ad55821d68c586cde2992b8d654e1e943363144e6d"
    },
    {
      "id": "C7-duration",
      "source_id": "sklearn-cross-validation",
      "text": "Indeed, the folds must represent the same duration, in order to have comparable metrics across folds.",
      "location": "Section 3.1.2.6.1 Time Series Split",
      "pdf_page": null,
      "extracted_text_offset": 34589,
      "raw_sha256": "78d7587fa92ba3b3e480c9d841b50fedc14ac29d571ccb319d4068235154f0e2",
      "extracted_text_sha256": "009ce290e0897fddf43ed8ad55821d68c586cde2992b8d654e1e943363144e6d"
    }
